  "question": "1. Background / Context\n\nLaravel Spark is a SaaS subscription billing solution specifically designed for Laravel applications. It builds upon the Laravel Cashier package and integrates with Stripe as a subscription payment gateway. Spark provides a complete set of tools including a dedicated customer billing portal. This facilitates the management of subscription plans and payments, streamlining the billing process for SaaS businesses.\n\n 2. Objectives\n\nThe primary objective of Laravel Spark is to simplify subscription billing management for SaaS applications by offering a full-featured solution that supports various billing scenarios such as recurring payments and per-seat pricing. It aims to provide seamless integration with Stripe and PayPal for handling payments.\n\n 3. Stakeholders & Users\n\n- SaaS Business Owners: Need a robust and reliable billing solution to manage subscription plans and customer billing.\n- Customers: Require an intuitive billing portal to manage their subscriptions and payments.\n- Developers: Utilize Spark to shorten development time by using a pre-built billing solution.\n\n 4. Functional Descriptions\n\n- Subscription Management: Define and manage subscription plans (monthly/yearly) via a configuration file.\n- Customer Billing Portal: Provides customers with a portal to subscribe, update plans, update payment information, and download invoices.\n- Billing and Payments: Supports Stripe and PayPal (via Paddle) for processing recurring payments.\n- Invoice Generation: Customers can download invoices in PDF format and receive them via email.\n- Per-Seat Billing: Supports billing customers based on the number of seats (users/projects).\n- Frontend Flexibility: The billing portal is isolated and includes its own frontend assets, allowing for flexible integration with any frontend technology.\n- Easy Upgrades: The isolated nature of the billing portal allows for straightforward updates without impacting the main application.\n\n 5. Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Designed to handle a large number of subscriptions and user interactions efficiently.\n- Security: Processes payments securely using Stripe's and PayPal's existing security features.\n- Usability: Provides a user-friendly interface for both customers and administrators for managing subscriptions and billing activities.\n- Integration: Seamlessly integrates with existing Laravel applications, leveraging the Laravel ecosystem.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0085\nCREATE TABLE `subscriptions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stripe_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stripe_price` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trial_ends_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ends_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `subscriptions_user_id_index` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `subscription_items` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `subscription_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stripe_product` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stripe_price` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `subscription_items_subscription_id_index` (`subscription_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscription_items_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`subscription_id`) REFERENCES `subscriptions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `invoices` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `host` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tax` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `currency` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `invoice_pdf` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `invoices_user_id_index` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invoices_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
